
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>CSS Overflow, Transform and Transition</title>

<style>
* {
    box-sizing: border-box;
}

body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 20px;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    background: #f1f5f9;
    color: #1e293b;
}

h1 {
    text-align: center;
}

h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-size: 20px;
}

.section {
    background: white;
    padding: 18px;
    margin: 20px auto;
    max-width: 1000px;
    border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
    border-radius: 8px;
}

.example {
    background: #eff6ff;
    border: 1px solid #bfdbfe;
    padding: 12px;
    margin: 10px 0;
    border-radius: 5px;
}

.label {
    color: #9a3412;
    font-family: monospace;
    font-weight: bold;
}

.demo {
    background: #2563eb;
    color: white;
    padding: 12px;
    margin: 8px 0;
    border-radius: 4px;
}

/* OVERFLOW EXAMPLES */

.overflow-box {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 280px;
    height: 65px;
    background: #dbeafe;
    border: 2px solid #2563eb;
    padding: 8px;
    margin: 12px 0;
}

.visible {
    overflow: visible;
}

.hidden {
    overflow: hidden;
}

.scroll {
    overflow: scroll;
}

.auto {
    overflow: auto;
}

.overflow-x {
    overflow-x: auto;
    overflow-y: hidden;
    white-space: nowrap;
}

.overflow-x span {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 120px;
    background: #2563eb;
    color: white;
    padding: 10px;
    margin-right: 5px;
}

.ellipsis {
    width: 250px;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    background: #dbeafe;
    padding: 10px;
    border: 1px solid #2563eb;
}

/* TRANSFORM EXAMPLES */

.transform-box {
    width: 130px;
    height: 65px;
    background: #059669;
    color: white;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    margin: 20px 10px;
    border-radius: 5px;
}

.translate {
    transform: translate(20px, 5px);
}

.rotate {
    transform: rotate(8deg);
}

.scale {
    transform: scale(1.1);
}

.scale-x {
    transform: scaleX(1.2);
}

.scale-y {
    transform: scaleY(1.2);
}

.skew {
    transform: skew(10deg, 0deg);
}

.origin {
    transform: rotate(12deg);
    transform-origin: left center;
}

.combined {
    transform: translateX(10px) rotate(5deg) scale(1.05);
}

/* TRANSITION EXAMPLES */

.transition-box {
    width: 150px;
    background: #7c3aed;
    color: white;
    padding: 15px;
    margin: 12px 0;
    text-align: center;
    border-radius: 5px;
    cursor: pointer;
}

.transition-box:hover {
    background: #db2777;
    transform: translateX(20px) scale(1.05);
}

.duration {
    transition-property: transform, background-color;
    transition-duration: 0.5s;
}

.timing {
    transition: transform 0.5s ease-in-out;
}

.delay {
    transition: transform 0.4s ease 0.5s;
}

.all {
    transition: all 0.4s ease;
}

.all:hover {
    padding-left: 35px;
}

table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: 10px;
}

th, td {
    border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
    padding: 9px;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
}

th {
    background: #dbeafe;
}

@media (max-width: 600px) {
    body {
        padding: 10px;
    }

    th, td {
        padding: 6px;
        font-size: 13px;
    }
}
</style>
</head>

<body>

<h1>CSS Overflow, Transform & Transition</h1>
<p style="text-align:center">
    Simple properties, examples and explanations
</p>

<!-- OVERFLOW -->

<section class="section">
<h2>PART 1: CSS OVERFLOW</h2>
<p>Overflow controls what happens when content is bigger than its box.</p>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">1. overflow: visible;</div>
    <p>Extra content can appear outside the box.</p>
    <div class="overflow-box visible">
        This is long content that can continue outside the fixed-height box.
        The extra text remains visible.
    </div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">2. overflow: hidden;</div>
    <p>Extra content outside the box is clipped.</p>
    <div class="overflow-box hidden">
        This is long content. The remaining text is hidden because the box
        has a fixed height and overflow is hidden.
    </div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">3. overflow: scroll;</div>
    <p>Scrollbars are provided so the content can be viewed.</p>
    <div class="overflow-box scroll">
        This is long content. Scroll inside this box to read more.
        This is another line. This is another line. This is another line.
        This is another line.
    </div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">4. overflow: auto;</div>
    <p>Scrollbars appear when they are needed.</p>
    <div class="overflow-box auto">
        This is long content. Scroll inside this box to read more.
        This is another line. This is another line. This is another line.
    </div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">5. overflow-x: auto;</div>
    <p>Allows horizontal scrolling when content is too wide.</p>
    <div class="overflow-box overflow-x">
        <span>Item 1</span><span>Item 2</span><span>Item 3</span>
        <span>Item 4</span>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">6. overflow-y: auto;</div>
    <p>Controls vertical overflow. A vertical scrollbar appears when needed.</p>
    <div class="overflow-box" style="overflow-x:hidden; overflow-y:auto">
        Line 1<br>Line 2<br>Line 3<br>Line 4<br>Line 5<br>Line 6
    </div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">7. text-overflow: ellipsis;</div>
    <p>Shows three dots when clipped text does not fit on one line.</p>
    <div class="ellipsis">
        This is a very long line of text that will be shortened with dots.
    </div>
</div>

<table>
<tr><th>Property / Value</th><th>Easy explanation</th></tr>
<tr><td>overflow</td><td>Controls content that exceeds its box.</td></tr>
<tr><td>visible</td><td>Extra content can appear outside the box.</td></tr>
<tr><td>hidden</td><td>Clips content outside the box.</td></tr>
<tr><td>scroll</td><td>Provides scrolling in the box.</td></tr>
<tr><td>auto</td><td>Adds scrolling when needed.</td></tr>
<tr><td>overflow-x</td><td>Controls horizontal overflow.</td></tr>
<tr><td>overflow-y</td><td>Controls vertical overflow.</td></tr>
<tr><td>text-overflow</td><td>Controls how clipped inline text is displayed.</td></tr>
<tr><td>white-space: nowrap</td><td>Keeps text on one line.</td></tr>
</table>
</section>

<!-- TRANSFORM -->

<section class="section">
<h2>PART 2: CSS TRANSFORM</h2>
<p>Transform moves, rotates, enlarges, shrinks or tilts an element.</p>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">1. transform: translate(20px, 5px);</div>
    <p>Moves an element horizontally and vertically.</p>
    <div class="transform-box translate">Translate</div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">2. transform: rotate(8deg);</div>
    <p>Rotates an element.</p>
    <div class="transform-box rotate">Rotate</div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">3. transform: scale(1.1);</div>
    <p>Enlarges an element to 110% of its original size.</p>
    <div class="transform-box scale">Scale</div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">4. transform: scaleX(1.2);</div>
    <p>Enlarges an element horizontally.</p>
    <div class="transform-box scale-x">Scale X</div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">5. transform: scaleY(1.2);</div>
    <p>Enlarges an element vertically.</p>
    <div class="transform-box scale-y">Scale Y</div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">6. transform: skew(10deg, 0deg);</div>
    <p>Tilts an element along an axis.</p>
    <div class="transform-box skew">Skew</div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">7. transform-origin: left center;</div>
    <p>Changes the point around which an element rotates or transforms.</p>
    <div class="transform-box origin">Origin</div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">8. Combine multiple transforms</div>
    <p>Use translate(), rotate() and scale() together.</p>
    <div class="transform-box combined">Combined</div>
</div>

<table>
<tr><th>Property / Function</th><th>Easy explanation</th></tr>
<tr><td>transform</td><td>Applies a visual transformation.</td></tr>
<tr><td>translate(x, y)</td><td>Moves an element.</td></tr>
<tr><td>translateX()</td><td>Moves an element horizontally.</td></tr>
<tr><td>translateY()</td><td>Moves an element vertically.</td></tr>
<tr><td>rotate()</td><td>Rotates an element.</td></tr>
<tr><td>scale()</td><td>Changes width and height visually.</td></tr>
<tr><td>scaleX()</td><td>Changes horizontal size visually.</td></tr>
<tr><td>scaleY()</td><td>Changes vertical size visually.</td></tr>
<tr><td>skew()</td><td>Tilts an element.</td></tr>
<tr><td>transform-origin</td><td>Sets the transformation's origin point.</td></tr>
<tr><td>none</td><td>Applies no transformation.</td></tr>
</table>
</section>

<!-- TRANSITION -->

<section class="section">
<h2>PART 3: CSS TRANSITION</h2>
<p>Transition makes changes between CSS states happen smoothly.</p>
<p><strong>Hover over each purple box to test it.</strong></p>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">
        1. transition-property: transform, background-color;
        <br>
        transition-duration: 0.5s;
    </div>
    <div class="transition-box duration">Hover over me</div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">
        2. transition: transform 0.5s ease-in-out;
    </div>
    <div class="transition-box timing">Hover over me</div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">
        3. transition: transform 0.4s ease 0.5s;
    </div>
    <p>The transform starts after a half-second delay.</p>
    <div class="transition-box delay">Hover over me</div>
</div>

<div class="example">
    <div class="label">
        4. transition: all 0.4s ease;
    </div>
    <p>Transitions all supported CSS properties that change.</p>
    <div class="transition-box all">Hover over me</div>
</div>

<table>
<tr><th>Property / Value</th><th>Easy explanation</th></tr>
<tr><td>transition</td><td>Shorthand for transition settings.</td></tr>
<tr><td>transition-property</td><td>Chooses which CSS properties to animate.</td></tr>
<tr><td>transition-duration</td><td>Sets how long the transition takes.</td></tr>
<tr><td>transition-timing-function</td><td>Controls the speed pattern of the transition.</td></tr>
<tr><td>ease</td><td>Starts and ends more slowly.</td></tr>
<tr><td>linear</td><td>Uses a constant speed.</td></tr>
<tr><td>ease-in</td><td>Starts slowly.</td></tr>
<tr><td>ease-out</td><td>Ends slowly.</td></tr>
<tr><td>ease-in-out</td><td>Starts and ends slowly.</td></tr>
<tr><td>transition-delay</td><td>Waits before the transition starts.</td></tr>
</table>
</section>

</body>
</html>
